    <briefdescription>
<para>One reading of the manifest, run on the pool. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>It holds the results until the message thread applies them.</para>
<para>The job parses and validates the manifest. A valid manifest gives the toolchain child, the roots child, and the timeout and threads values from the daemon table. A failed validation gives an empty toolchain child carrying the message property, the project roots, and the default timeout and thread count. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
